      "text": "To solve the system of equations:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n3x - 5y &= -11, \\quad \\text{(1)} \\\\\n7x + 2y &= -12, \\quad \\text{(2)}\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nwe can use the method of elimination or substitution. Here, we'll use the elimination method. \n\nFirst, we need to eliminate one of the variables. To do this, we will make the coefficients of either \\(x\\) or \\(y\\) opposites. Let's eliminate \\(y\\). We can achieve this by finding a common multiple of the coefficients of \\(y\\) in both equations, which are \\(-5\\) and \\(2\\). The least common multiple of \\(5\\) and \\(2\\) is \\(10\\).\n\nWe'll multiply equation (1) by \\(2\\) and equation (2) by \\(5\\) to make the coefficients of \\(y\\) opposites:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n2(3x - 5y) &= 2(-11), \\\\\n5(7x + 2y) &= 5(-12).\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n6x - 10y &= -22, \\\\\n35x + 10y &= -60.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nNow, we add these two new equations together to eliminate \\(y\\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n6x - 10y + 35x + 10y &= -22 - 60, \\\\\n41x &= -82.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-82}{41}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we will substitute \\(x = \\frac{-82}{41}\\) back into one of the original equations to solve for \\(y\\). We'll substitute into equation (1):\n\n\\[\n3\\left(\\frac{-82}{41}\\right) - 5y = -11.\n\\]\n\nLet's solve this for \\(y\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{-246}{41} - 5y = -11,\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-5y = -11 + \\frac{246}{41},\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-5y = \\frac{-451 + 246}{41}.\n\\]\n\nCombining the numerators:\n\n\\[\n-5y = \\frac{-205}{41},\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\ny = \\frac{205}{41 \\cdot 5} = \\frac{205}{205} = 1.\n\\]\n\nSo the solution to the system of equations is \\( (x, y) = \\left(\\frac{-82}{41}, 1\\right) \\).\n\nFinally, we'll box our answers:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\left(-\\frac{82}{41}, 1\\right)}\n\\]\n\nLet's check our answers with Python.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\r\n\r\n# Define the symbols\r\nx, y = symbols('x y')\r\n\r\n# Define the equations\r\neq1 = Eq(3*x - 5*y, -11)\r\neq2 = Eq(7*x + 2*y, -12)\r\n\r\n# Solve the system of equations\r\nsolution = solve((eq1, eq2), (x, y))\r\nprint(solution)\n```",
