      "text": "To solve the system of equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n3x - 5y &= -11, \\\\\n7x + 2y &= -12,\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\nwe can use the method of elimination. The first step is to eliminate one of the variables by finding a common multiple of the coefficients of the \\(x\\) or \\(y\\) terms in the equations.\n\n**Step 1: Eliminate \\(y\\).**\n\nTo eliminate \\(y\\), we need to make the coefficients of \\(y\\) in both equations equal. The least common multiple of 5 and 2 is 10. We will multiply the first equation by 2 and the second equation by 5 to achieve this.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n2(3x - 5y) &= 2(-11), \\\\\n5(7x + 2y) &= 5(-12).\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n6x - 10y &= -22, \\\\\n35x + 10y &= -60.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Add the two equations.**\n\nNow, add the two equations to eliminate \\(y\\):\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n(6x - 10y) + (35x + 10y) &= -22 + (-60), \\\\\n6x + 35x &= -82, \\\\\n41x &= -82.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Solve for \\(x\\).**\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nx &= \\frac{-82}{41}, \\\\\nx &= -2.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n**Step 4: Substitute \\(x = -2\\) back into one of the original equations to solve for \\(y\\).**\n\nWe can use the first equation \\(3x - 5y = -11\\):\n\\[\n3(-2) - 5y = -11.\n\\]\n\n**Step 5: Simplify and solve for \\(y\\).**\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n-6 - 5y &= -11, \\\\\n-5y &= -11 + 6, \\\\\n-5y &= -5, \\\\\ny &= 1.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nSo, the solution to the system of equations is the ordered pair \\((-2, 1)\\).\n\nThe solution is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(-2, 1)}\n\\]",
